  "name": "Aftermarket appetite (IPO ETF vs SPY)",
  "notes": "**What it shows.** Whether investors are rewarding recent IPOs — the Renaissance IPO ETF measured against SPY. A rising line means the recent-issue basket is outperforming the broad market, a sign of healthy aftermarket appetite for new deals; a falling one means new issues are out of favor.\n\n**How it's computed.** The daily close of the Renaissance IPO ETF (ticker IPO) ÷ the SPY close, indexed to 100 on 2024-01-02. The anchor date is fixed so the level's meaning doesn't drift as the data window moves.\n\n**Caveats.** A rebased relative-strength ratio — read moves against the anchor date, not the absolute number.",
